G2819.def:
κλῆρος, -ου, ὁ 
[in LXX chiefly for נַחֲלָה גּוֹרָל ;] 
a lot; 
__(a) that which is cast or drawn: Matthieu 27:35, Marc 15:24, Luc 23:34, Jean 19:24" (LXX), Actes 1:26; 
__(b) that which is obtained by casting: Actes 1:17 8:21; of a part in the Kingdom of God (cf. Wis 55), Actes 26:18, Colossiens 1:12; pl. of the "cure" of a presbyter, 1 Pierre 5:3 (see ICC, in l).†

G2822.def:
κλητός, -ή, -όν
(καλέω), [in LXX for קָרָא, מִקְרָא, Exode 12:16, al. ;] 
called, invited (as to a banquet, Æsch., 1Sa 1:41, 3Ma.5:14); in NT, always of the Divine call; 
__(a) to some office: κ. ἀπόστολος, Romains 1:1, 1 Corinthiens 1:1; 
__(b) to salvation: Romains 8:28, 1 Corinthiens 1:24, Ju 1; κ. καὶ ἐκλεκτοὶ κ. πιστοί, Apocalypse 17:14; in gosp. (not in pl., see: καλέω) disting. fr.ἐκλεκτός, Matthieu 20:16 (WH, txt., R, omit), Matthieu 22:14; κ. Ἰησοῦ Χρ., Romains 1:6; κ. ἅγιοι, saints by calling, Romains 1:7, 1 Corinthiens 1:2.†
